Z||000000||wkayl||07-04-2001||09:14 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.winlambo.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.winlambo.com/</A> <BR>Here it is to be given away.  The news is that it is a replica built on an 88 Fiero.<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg"> <BR>Dnyee's 88 Formula, Casey's 86GT, Wayne's 86GT.  <BR>We consider my wife as being "Fiero Challenged"||||reg||1
Z||000001||TRiAD||07-04-2001||11:47 AM||||Nothing compares to Euro-Works, Ltd. <BR>I've been a Lamborghini fan since birth, and the Countach was the epitome of my desire. A well thought-out Euro-Works car would convince me until you popped the decklid. <P>It's hard to beat "free" though, ain't it?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||8Ball||07-04-2001||10:01 PM||||It isn't free you Have to send the guy a check for 35 dollars to enter.<P>And in another part of the page, the guy has posted an email he recieved asking how many times you were allowed to enter. the guy replied you can enter a MINIMUM of 1500 times to win and a max of 10,000 to win||||reg||1
Z||000003||gabriel||07-05-2001||05:24 PM||||Greets:<P>&gt; Nothing compares to Euro-Works, Ltd. <P>  Sure it does.  Ever see this kit?<P>   <A HREF="http://www.kitcar.com/exotic/home.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kitcar.com/exotic/home.html</A>           <BR>   Euro-Works is one fine kit though ... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>The idea of having all that extra room for an engine swap is interesting, isn't it?||||reg||1
Z||000004||TRiAD||07-05-2001||05:51 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.kitcar.com/exotic/ExoticIllusRed2b.jpg"> <P>Nice, but it does not correctly emulate the windows, bumpers, rear end dimensions, and many other aspects of the Countach. <P>This, on the other hand...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.watsonstudios.com/lambo/nice1bg.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.watsonstudios.com/lambo/nice9bg.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.watsonstudios.com/lambo/nice3bg.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.watsonstudios.com/lambo/nice10bg.jpg"> <P>...nearly perfectly emulates almost every detail of the Countach. <P>IF I were to do a "replica", it would have to be 99% correct, or I'd do something that's just a "kit", and not a replica of anything. But that's just me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000005||gabriel||07-06-2001||10:28 AM||||&gt;IF I were to do a "replica", it would have to be 99% correct, <P>  Have to agree with you there - Thats why my TR is taking so long - I'm still looking for correct glass for the windshield & rear window.(<I>try</I> to find them)  And that Countach there is one d@mn sweet car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>BTW, what is different about the windows between Euro & Exotic?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||07-06-2001||01:02 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 8Ball:<BR><B>It isn't free you Have to send the guy a check for 35 dollars to enter.<P>And in another part of the page, the guy has posted an email he recieved asking how many times you were allowed to enter. the guy replied you can enter a MINIMUM of 1500 times to win and a max of 10,000 to win</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The way the Email is posted is confusing. But if you read the rules and regs page it says they have to have 1500 entries in order for the contest to proceed. If they don't get 1500 entries then your money is refunded minus a 10% fee. So in order for the contest to be valid they need 1500 entries from 1500 people, (assuming that each person enters once) but after 10,000 entries are received they won't accept any more.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 07-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||TRiAD||07-06-2001||02:59 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by gabriel:<BR><B>...what is different about the windows between Euro & Exotic?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If you look right above the mirror on the "Exotic", you'll notice a few things...<P>1) The front corner window terminates in a flat edge on the leading point, on the "Euro" and the real ones, there is a piece of black trim there instead of just regular "body". <P>2) On the "Exotic", the other 2 pieces of the side window are just one piecs, as attested by the reflections in the "warp" of the plexi. On the "Euro", and the real one, this is made of 2 seperate pieces, and is real tinted glass, not plexi. <P>3) On the "Exotic, the front bumper is completely flat from left to right, "Euro" and real are slightly curved. <P>4) Vents in the front bumper are wrong on the "Exotic".<P>5-8) Front skits vent, side skirt vent, and NACA duct are open on Euro and real, not on the Exotic, and the Fuel "cap" is wrong on the Exotic. <P>9) The Exotic is short-wheelbase. The Euro is OE wheelbase. (matches the real thing with a frame-stretch). <P>10) Back end on the Exotic is completely wrong...there's just way too much to list there...<P>Anyway, you get the idea...It's basically just a "Kit".  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||gabriel||07-06-2001||03:31 PM||||Wow!  you really know your Lambos!<P>I did think that EI made both a stretched and an unstretched model though.  Have you ever seen this site?<P>   <A HREF="http://www.exoticrebodies.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.exoticrebodies.com/</A> <P>I believe that one of the kitcar mags just featured one of their cars.   - Now if I could just get some info on Ferrari glass, I'd be happy ....||||reg||1
Z||000009||dman||07-06-2001||04:35 PM||||Hello everyone. Gabriel, I've been following the progress of your kit car and I must say you are doing an awesome job.<P>I have a friend that has several Ferrari Testarossa windshields. If you are interested in using them for your TR project email me. Since they are genuine they won't be cheap however there are several alternatives. Email me for more info.<P>||||reg||1
